 \, Ap\n\nLives of the Saints — THE CONVERSION OF ST. PAUL: THE great apo
 stle Paul, named Saul at his circumcision, was born at Tarsus, the capital
  of Silicia, and was by privilege a Roman citizen, to which quality a grea
 t distinction and several exemptions were granted by the laws of the empir
 e.
