SUMMARY:St. Romuald\, Ab (d)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nFirst Saturday of the Month\n\nLives of 
 the Saints — ST. ROMUALD, Abbot: In 976, Sergius, a nobleman of Eavenna,
  quarrelled with a relative about an estate, and slew him in a duel. His s
 on Eomuald, horrified at his father's crime, entered the Benedictine monas
 tery at Classe, to do a forty days' penance for him.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
