SUMMARY:Our Lady's Saturday (sp)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nSt. Valentine\, Priest\, M\n\nLives of t
 he Saints — ST. VALENTINE, Priest and Martyr: St. Valentine was a lioly 
 priest in Pome, who, with St. Marius and his family, assisted the martyrs 
 in the persecution under Claudius II. He was apprehended, and sent by the 
 emperor to the prefect of Pome, who, on finding all his promises to make h
 im renounce his faith ineffectual, commanded him to be beaten with clubs, 
 and afterward to be beheaded, which was executed on the 14th of February, 
 about the year 270.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
