DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260701
SUMMARY:Commemoration of St. Paul\, Ap (dm)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nSt. Peter\, Ap\nWithin the Octave\n\nHis
 torical note — Father Lasance Missal: This day gives special honor to St
 . Paul\, whose writings continue his apostolic preaching throughout the Ch
 urch.\n\nLives of the Saints — ST. PAUL: St. Paul was born at Tarsus, of
  Jewish parents, and studied, at Jerusalem, at the feet of Gamaliel. While
  still a young man, he held the clothes of those who stoned the proto-mart
 yr Stephen; and in his restless zeal he pressed on to Damascus, "breathing
  out threatenings and slaughter against the disciples of Christ." But near
  Damascus a light from heaven struck him to the earth.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
