 ts — ST. MARGARET, Virgin and Martyr: ac CORDING to the ancient Martyrol
 ogies, St. Margaret suffered at Antioch in Pisidia, in the last general pe
 rsecution. She is said to have been instructed in the Faith by a Christian
  nurse, to have been persecuted by her own father, a pagan priest, and, af
 ter many torments, to have gloriously finished her martyrdom by the sword.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
