SUMMARY:ST. JAMES THE GREATER\, Ap (d2cl)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nSt. Christopher\, M\n\nLives of the Sain
 ts — ST. JAMES, Apostle: St. James was one. He alone, with Peter and Joh
 n, was admitted to the house of Jairus when the dead maiden was raised to 
 life. They alone were taken up to the high mountain apart, and saw the fac
 e of Jesus shining as the sun, and His garments white as snow; and these t
 hree alone witnessed the fearful agony in Gethsemane.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
