 ctor: St. Jerome was sent to school at Eome. His boyhood was not free from
  fault. His thirst for knowledge was excessive, and his love of books a pa
 ssion. He had studied under the best masters, visited foreign cities, and 
 devoted himself to the pursuit of science.
