DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:St. Clement I\, PM (d)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nSt. Felicitas\, M\n\nHistorical note —
  Father Lasance Missal: St. Clement\, an early Pope and martyr\, is named 
 in the Roman Canon and is linked with the ancient basilica of San Clemente
  in Rome.\n\nLives of the Saints — ST. CLEMENT OF ROME: T. Clement is sa
 id to have been a convert of noble birth, and to have been consecrated bis
 hop by St. Peter himself. With the words of the apostles still ringing in 
 his ears, he began to rule the Church of God ; and thus he was among the f
 irst, as he was among the m.ost illustrious, in the long line of those who
  have held the place and power of Peter.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-821b81f0-e71b-5d09-9d8e-9aa26626e521@traditional-calendar-20
 26
DTSTAMP:20260726T203036Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T220841Z
SEQUENCE:6
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:St. John of the Cross\, CD (d)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: White\n\nSt. Chrysogonus\, M\n\nLives of the Sa
 ints — ST. JOHN OF THE CROSS: St. John of the Cross was discarded by his
  kindred Vi for marrying a poor orphan, and the Saint, thus born and nurtu
 red in poverty, chose it also for his portion. Unable to learn a trade, be
  became the servant of the poor in the hospital of Medina, while still pur
 suing his sacred studies.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-25-6bdebf28-084e-59a2-8991-91bced60c553@traditional-calendar-20
