SUMMARY:St. Ambrose\, BpCD (d)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: White\n\nVigil of the Immaculate Conception of 
 the BVM\nFast & Complete Abstinence\n\nLives of the Saints — ST. AMBROSE
 , Bishop: St. Ambrose was of a noble family, and was governor of Milan in 
 374, when a bishop was to be chosen for that great see. As the Arian heret
 ics were many and fierce, he was present to preserve order during the elec
 tion. Though only a catechumen, it was the will of God that he should hims
 elf be chosen by acclamation; and, in spite of his utmost resistance, he w
 as baptized and consecrated.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
